  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Xperi is in the early stages of a strategic pivot from licensing toward advertising monetization, with its Media Platform showing accelerating momentum. The TiVo One ad platform is rapidly scaling its monthly active user base as enhanced targeting and measurement capabilities roll out, while the DTS AutoStage footprint in connected vehicles continues to expand. Overall revenue remains stable as the mix shifts, with the ad-driven segment beginning to inflect. The narrative challenges persistent bearish views by illustrating real product-led traction in connected TV and automotive end markets, though the business still operates near breakeven on a bottom-line basis.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is executing a clear plan: scale the TiVo One ad platform, deepen engagement with AutoStage, and pivot the revenue model toward higher-growth monetization streams. The team reaffirmed full-year guidance and signaled a path to positive free cash flow, underscoring confidence in the trajectory. They are investing in ad product improvements and direct sales programs, while managing costs to narrow losses. The tone on earnings calls is one of inflection, with management highlighting that key milestones are being met, though credibility will hinge on sustaining user growth and converting it into durable revenue gains as the year progresses.",
